issue.body:
When validating these lines of javascript:

``` javascript
var func = function (first, ...rest) {
  return rest
}

func(1, 2, 3)
```

with this .eslintrc config:

``` javascript
{
    "rules": {
        "strict": false,
        "semi": 0
     },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "restParams": true,
        "spread": true
    }
}
```

I still get the following errors:

```
restParams.js
  1:21  error  first is defined but never used  no-unused-vars
  2:9   error  'rest' is not defined        no-undef

✖ 2 problems (2 errors, 0 warnings)
```

The rule doesn't seem to realize that there is a second parameter named 'rest' in the function declaration.

As I understand ESLint doesn’t understand that `import` create variable.

So I get a `'Warning' is not defined` error on line 2 of this code:

``` js
import Warning from '../lib/warning';
var warn = new Warning('text');
```

I uses eslint 0.16.1 and my `.eslintrc` is:

``` js
{
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "modules": true,
        "module":  true
    },
    "env": {
        "mocha": true,
        "node":  true,
        "es6":   true
    }
}
```

/cc @nzakas 
