Hi all,
I've tried to make this bit of code good enough for ESlint rule `prefer-rest-params` but I ran out of ideas. 
The problem is with the line `this._super(...arguments);`
Any help would be appreciated. Thanks
```
didTransition() {
    this._super(...arguments);
    Ember.run.scheduleOnce('afterRender', this, () => {
      this._trackPage(this.get('url'), document.title);
    });
  },
```

@Willibaur The spread operator needs to be used on a defined variable. Usually, you would do so by declaring a rest parameter in the method definition.

Try this:

```js
  didTransition(...args) { // <-- Variable definition: args
    this._super(...args);
    Ember.run.scheduleOnce('afterRender', this, () => {
      this._trackPage(this.get('url'), document.title);
    });
  },
```

If you still have trouble or have any follow-ups, please create a new issue or stop by our [Gitter chat](https://gitter.im/eslint/eslint). Thanks!
